{"type":"plan","title":"風鈴の願い","logline":"夏の京都、祖母の風鈴が再び鳴るまで、少女の小さな願いが夜風に乗る。","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide shot of the engawa veranda in bright summer noon, sunlight filtering through shoji onto the wooden floor; Yui steps onto the veranda carrying a small bag while Grandma sits on a cushion near the silent furin.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"夏休み、ゆいは、京都のおばあちゃんの家に、遊びに来ました。","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot focusing on the Edo furin hanging from the eave, perfectly still in the midday sun; Yui leans in, looking closely at the silent chime.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"縁側には、古い江戸風鈴が、ひとつ下がっていますが、もう、音が鳴りません。","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Over-the-shoulder close-up of Grandma speaking, her hands resting on her lap; Yui's face turns toward her, listening intently.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おじいちゃんと買った風鈴なの」と、おばあちゃんは、言いました。","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low-angle wide shot of the Gion festival street at dusk, lanterns glowing amber; Yui and Grandma in matching yukata walk side by side toward the bustling stalls.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"夕方、二人は、浴衣を着て、祇園祭の宵山へ、出かけました。","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Slow pan along the lantern-lit stalls, paper lanterns swaying gently, crowds of yukata-clad visitors moving between food stands.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"提灯の灯る通りには、屋台が、ずらりと並んでいます。","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot at a furin stall: Yui's hand selects a single blue tanzaku strip from a wooden tray, the paper catching the lantern light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"風鈴の屋台で、ゆいは、青い短冊を、一枚選びました。","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Slow zoom-in into the tatami tea room at night, paper lanterns casting warm pools; Yui sits at the low table, writing her wish on the blue tanzaku.","mode":"still","dialogue":"夜、家に帰ると、ゆいは、短冊に、願いごとを書きました。","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Extreme close-up of the blue tanzaku, the handwritten wish visible: “おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように”.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように」。","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot on the veranda at night: Yui ties the blue tanzaku to the Edo furin; a gentle night breeze stirs the chime, the red tassel swaying.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ゆいが、短冊を風鈴に結ぶと、夜風が、そっと吹きました。","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up of the furin as it rings — a clear “ちりん” — the glass tube vibrating, the red tassel dancing in the lantern glow.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ちりん。風鈴が、ひさしぶりに、鳴りました。","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot on the veranda under lantern light: Grandma wipes a tear from her cheek and gently places her hand on Yui's head, both smiling through tears.","mode":"still","dialogue":"おばあちゃんは、そっと涙をふいて、ゆいの頭を、なでました。","cites":[]}]}
